# VS Code REST Client examples. Use an APIM subscription ID configuration and a valid
# subscription key supplied only in your personal, untracked REST Client environment.
# Model and operation names must match the configured APIM API and price cards.
@gateway = https://your-gateway.azure-api.net

### Non-streaming: APIM reserves, backend executes, actual usage settles
POST {{gateway}}/foundry/chat/completions
Content-Type: application/json
Ocp-Apim-Subscription-Key: {{$processEnv APIM_SUBSCRIPTION_KEY}}

{
  "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "Explain why budget caps differ from TPM limits."}],
  "max_tokens": 64,
  "stream": false
}

### Streaming: conservative reservation, no client-supplied cache discount
POST {{gateway}}/foundry/chat/completions
Content-Type: application/json
Ocp-Apim-Subscription-Key: {{$processEnv APIM_SUBSCRIPTION_KEY}}

{
  "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "Describe cached input token pricing."}],
  "max_tokens": 64,
  "stream": true
}

### OpenAI Responses: stateless inline input, bounded output
POST {{gateway}}/foundry/responses
Content-Type: application/json
Ocp-Apim-Subscription-Key: {{$processEnv APIM_SUBSCRIPTION_KEY}}

{
  "model": "sample-model",
  "input": "Explain why token budgets and dollar budgets differ.",
  "max_output_tokens": 64,
  "store": false,
  "stream": false
}

### OpenAI Responses: streaming retains conservative reservation
POST {{gateway}}/foundry/responses
Content-Type: application/json
Ocp-Apim-Subscription-Key: {{$processEnv APIM_SUBSCRIPTION_KEY}}

{
  "model": "sample-model",
  "input": "Describe cached input token pricing.",
  "max_output_tokens": 64,
  "store": false,
  "stream": true
}

### Anthropic Messages: explicit cache breakpoint; backend model/version are operator-pinned
POST {{gateway}}/anthropic/v1/messages
Content-Type: application/json
Ocp-Apim-Subscription-Key: {{$processEnv APIM_SUBSCRIPTION_KEY}}
anthropic-version: {{$processEnv ANTHROPIC_API_VERSION}}

{
  "model": "sample-claude",
  "max_tokens": 64,
  "system": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "You explain AI budget governance clearly. This short example does not guarantee a cache hit.",
      "cache_control": {"type": "ephemeral", "ttl": "5m"}
    }
  ],
  "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "Explain the distinction between cache reads and cache writes."}],
  "stream": false
}

### Anthropic Messages: streaming and 1-hour cache write pricing
POST {{gateway}}/anthropic/v1/messages
Content-Type: application/json
Ocp-Apim-Subscription-Key: {{$processEnv APIM_SUBSCRIPTION_KEY}}
anthropic-version: {{$processEnv ANTHROPIC_API_VERSION}}

{
  "model": "sample-claude",
  "max_tokens": 64,
  "system": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "You explain AI budget governance clearly. A real cacheable prefix must meet the model's minimum length.",
      "cache_control": {"type": "ephemeral", "ttl": "1h"}
    }
  ],
  "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "Explain conservative streaming accounting."}],
  "stream": true
}

### Language sentiment: record count rounds per document
POST {{gateway}}/language/sentiment
Content-Type: application/json
Ocp-Apim-Subscription-Key: {{$processEnv APIM_SUBSCRIPTION_KEY}}

{
  "documents": [
    {"id": "1", "language": "en", "text": "The example is easy to understand."},
    {"id": "2", "language": "en", "text": "The rate-limit decision is visible."}
  ]
}

### Document Intelligence: selected pages are enforced on the backend, not just claimed
POST {{gateway}}/document-intelligence/analyze?pages=1-2
Content-Type: application/json
Ocp-Apim-Subscription-Key: {{$processEnv APIM_SUBSCRIPTION_KEY}}

{
  "base64Source": "{{$processEnv SAMPLE_PDF_BASE64}}"
}

# Follow the returned gateway Operation-Location with the same identity.
# Do not call a raw backend URL or reuse another principal's operation ID.
